1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd8 4. d4 Nf6 5. Bc4 e6 6. Nf3 Bb4 7. O-O Nbd7 8.
Qe2 Bxc3 9. bxc3 O-O 10. Bg5 Re8 11. Ne5 Nf8 12. f4 c5 13. Rad1 Qd6 14. f5 Nd5
15. Nxf7 $1 Kxf7 16. fxe6+ Kg8 17. e7 Ne6 18. dxc5 Qxc5+ 19. Kh1 Nxc3 20. Rd8
$1 Bd7 {At this point Tal, without invitation, took one of Wally's cigarettes
and studied the position, then played} 21. Qe5 $3 {Tal passed on to the next
game. Wally, thinking he had made a blunder, called him back. Tal glanced back
at the board, smiled, and carried on to the next game.} Qxe5 ({The finish to
the game is given as} 21... Nd5 22. Qxd5 Qxd5 23. Rf8+ {1-0 in CHESS, April
1995, p27. (Letter from John McCormack, article by Larry Holmes, friends of
Wally Chandler at Liverpool CC. However, that finish is unsatisfactory as 23
Rf8+ would be a losing blunder and it seems unlikely that Tal would have
played it. JS}) 22. Rf8+ 1-0

